WEBVTT

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.250
Come on, beat him!

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:54.080
Punch his lights out!

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.160
Let's go!

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.010
That's right, get him!

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.010
You stupid...  attack his body!

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:00.770
Do you even see who you're fighting?

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:02.650
What are you doing? Use your legs!

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:03.230
You bastard!

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:04.680
Go get him!

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.580
It flew! It flew!

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.080
Look! Look at it!

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.110
It flew!

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.780
What did I tell you?

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.360
Wow!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.070
Go!{previous lines added by editor}

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:17.070
I got it!

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.120
All right, it's mine now!

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.070
Don't touch it!

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:22.160
Hurry up already, Joe!

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.160
It's my turn now! Come on!

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:28.160
Yeah, I know. Sachi, you're getting a cool jumbo jet.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.680
Whoa, there it goes!

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:34.670
Don't be in such a rush!

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.600
Hey! What do you brats think you're doing here?

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.460
This is the hallway for the competitors to enter and exit the stage!

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.650
Now get back to your seats!

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:48.940
And the same goes for you!

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.400
Come on, give it a rest!

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.260
Get in there!

00:02:54.260 --> 00:02:55.610
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

00:02:57.720 --> 00:03:00.210
Now settle down so I can give you a massage.

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:04.690
What, you think I'm a geezer? I don't need a massage!

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.170
My shoulders aren't even stiff!

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.350
That's not what I mean!

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:10.050
You need to relax your muscles.

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:11.910
You got that?

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.210
I don't need to loosen up!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.920
I've got a special body, you know!

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:24.620
I'm not some amateur that tenses up before a match!

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:26.430
I hope you're right...

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:29.080
Anyway, just lie down over there.

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:30.900
Nishi, grab the Vaseline!

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:41.030
Joe! Joe, is my plane ready yet?

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.680
Shut up already!

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.310
I told you, get to your seats!

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.500
You keep wasting your time with those brats...

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.550
Now, loosen up.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.220
Some special body you've got.

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:07.860
Your muscles and tendons are all rock-hard!

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:22.130
I guess even you would be pretty tense with the Rikiishi match ahead of you.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:27.160
Or maybe you're scared because it's Rikiishi?

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.380
Who are you callin' scared, old man?

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:32.540
Who's nervous!?

00:04:34.010 --> 00:04:35.950
Joe! Don't get so worked up!

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:47.790
Well, if you're not nervous, then there's nothing to worry about.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.140
But, Joe...

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:54.460
Your body must be getting nervous, even if your mind isn't.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.770
It's your instincts.

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:58.770
Instincts can be real frightening at times.

00:04:59.490 --> 00:05:02.960
Sometimes, they can even predict the future.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.950
Hey, Nishi. Go get the bandages and gloves ready.

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:10.620
Right!

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:16.120
What are you trying to say, old man?

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.640
Remember Rikiishi-kun at the weigh-in in the afternoon?

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.130
Didn't you feel it when you saw him?

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.130
Feel what?

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.320
He may have thinned out a lot,

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.140
but his skin wasn't deathly-pale like in the Pancho Leo match.

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.640
His complexion was healthier, and his face even had a tinge of red to it.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.610
That's right.

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:38.760
It really did.

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:42.000
Rikiishi had gone through a hellish weight loss,

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.320
but he...

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.820
Back there, he...

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:51.430
He looked for all the world like he was born with that body!

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:07.390
There, you're done.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.270
Nishi, get him ready! It's time!

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.090
Yes!

00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:33.740
The human body's a mysterious thing.

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.160
It takes on the qualities of its environment.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.470
So having endured hell itself,

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.630
Rikiishi-kun has made that hell his own.

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.090
Ain't that impressive?

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:54.270
Joe!

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.630
Spread your fingers, will you?

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:00.810
Yeah.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:11.330
<i>The match has ended at 1:58 in Round 5, with Yoshizawa winning by KO!</i>

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.830
Looks like the match before ours is done.

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:20.710
You see that counter I threw at him?

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:25.170
See, if I felt like it, I could've ended it after three rounds!

00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:54.240
O-Oh, yeah! I gotta hurry!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:58.250
Yeah, you're right! We gotta hurry!

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:27.190
Okay. Let's go, old man.

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:28.670
Yeah.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:39.180
Just listen to those ear-splitting cheers!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.310
The stands are bursting at the seams, with not a seat left empty!

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:47.040
But that said, what do you make of Rikiishi and Yabuki's post-juvie-

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:50.140
That is, their steadily-rising popularity?

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:55.280
Yeah, I'd say even the World Championship couldn't draw a crowd like this!

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:58.600
Because it represents the long-awaited showdown of destiny between Yabuki Joe and Rikiishi Toru,

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:01.530
this match is gathering more popularity and attention than the world title fight,

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:05.250
let alone the Japanese title fight!{please re-time per editing. could probably do just two lines, combining this one with the last one}

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.710
So, which one of them do you predict will win?

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.140
W-Well, that's a pretty hard question.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.300
I have a feeling it'll be Yabuki, but it could just as well be Rikiishi.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.480
Frankly, they both have a good chance.

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:17.820
It's anybody's fight?{maybe re-time previous line to make this an overlap}

00:10:17.820 --> 00:10:20.900
But either way, this will be a battle of wills.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:26.310
S-So I can only imagine that it'll end with a thrilling KO!

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:32.320
<i>We will now hold today's eight-round semifinal bantamweight match!</i>

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:36.330
<i>In the red corner, from Shiraki Gym,</i>

00:10:36.330 --> 00:10:38.150
<i>weighing in at 118 pounds...</i>

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.910
<i>Rikiishi Toru!</i>

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:52.740
<i>And in the blue corner, from Tange Gym,</i>

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.920
<i>weighing in at 117 and one-half pounds...</i>

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:59.430
<i>Yabuki Joe!</i>

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:07.940
All right!

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.270
Hey! Hey!

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:09.670
Hey, what's so funny, Rikiishi?

00:12:09.670 --> 00:12:11.440
What are you so happy about?

00:12:11.440 --> 00:12:12.080
Joe!

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:16.660
I don't get it at all!

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:17.730
Joe, what's gotten into you?

00:12:17.730 --> 00:12:19.750
I'm gonna fight you with all I have,

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.840
and you're just standing there, grinning at me?

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:35.020
Yabuki! Personal conversation in the ring is a foul!

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.280
How the hell could I be a boxer if I were afraid of fouls?

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:39.190
Yabuki!

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.820
Cut it out, Joe! What's the matter with you?

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:43.910
Let me make one thing clear.

00:12:44.770 --> 00:12:47.080
Get this through your skull, ref.

00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.890
Whoever wins this match...

00:12:53.270 --> 00:12:55.790
You probably think I'm modest for not saying I'm gonna win,

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.750
but whoever wins...

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.640
Joe, cut it out!

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:04.500
This match won't be settled by point deductions from fouls.

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:05.930
It'll end with a KO!

00:13:06.570 --> 00:13:09.220
Rikiishi Toru's matches are never won by points!

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:10.870
Never, you hear me? Never!

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:11.940
Never, you hear me? Never!

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.940
If you don't stop talking, I really will deduct points from you, Yabuki!

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.120
Fine by me! You can take your point deductions and shove-

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:20.130
Joe!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.750
Mind if I give him some advice before the match?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:35.290
I'm really sorry about this, Rikiishi-kun.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:40.960
Sit down!

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:43.720
What the hell were you thinking, Joe?

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:47.380
You were so solemn when you said your match with Rikiishi would be a showdown of destiny...

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.720
Why are you so damn combative now?

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.720
Screw seriousness and destiny. I can't box when I'm acting like a prude.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:14:00.400
Besides, this fight's meant to settle the score from our juvie days.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.690
So I ain't gonna hold back shit!

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.700
Hey! What are you mumbling about now?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.700
You're a sorry sight, Yabuki!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.120
Just lose already, Yabuki!

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:13.970
That's it, Rikiishi!

00:14:13.970 --> 00:14:16.340
Knock him to the mat! We'll be rooting for you!{split by editor}

00:14:16.340 --> 00:14:18.660
We're counting on you, Rikiishi!

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:23.520
Hey, Rikiishi! I can't say I dislike Yabuki, but if he's up against you, that's another story!

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:26.680
Rikiishi! Go ahead and beat Yabuki to a pulp!

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:28.440
Yeah, yeah! Yabuki's too rude!

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.390
Rikiishi Toru's the ideal boxer!

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.170
Take Yabuki down and become the champion!

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.810
We love you, Rikiishi!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:36.860
Yabuki can go die in a ditch!

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.810
You'll never land your Cross Counter on Rikiishi!

00:14:38.810 --> 00:14:41.170
You can't stand up to the future champion!

00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:43.450
Rikiishi's just too strong of a boxer!

00:14:43.450 --> 00:14:44.540
Bastards!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:45.150
Shut up!

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:45.740
Father!{previous lines added by editor}

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:49.700
What the hell? How the hell is Joe rude?

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.870
Father, please!

00:14:50.870 --> 00:14:53.910
Whoever said that, come on down! We'll teach you a lesson!

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.900
We're not gonna let you say whatever you want!

00:14:55.900 --> 00:14:57.870
I'll tear you all to shreds!

00:14:57.870 --> 00:15:00.370
Yabuki's cool because he's a brawler!

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.380
Yeah! Got a problem with that, assholes?

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:05.110
Yabuki, who cares what they say? I still got your back!

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:05.680
Joe!

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:07.380
Our 20th-century barbarian!

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.800
We love you, Yabuki!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:13.600
The bell hasn't even rung yet, and it already feels like the fight is underway!

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:15.410
Yeah, you said it!

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:17.380
You hardly see this kind of atmosphere nowadays,

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:23.140
what with the prevalence of "businessman boxers" and boxers built to be fighting machines.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:28.400
And I'm afraid... this mood is starting to feel suffocating.

00:15:32.730 --> 00:15:34.410
Old man, seconds gotta get out!

00:15:38.180 --> 00:15:42.170
Listen, Joe. When you're dodging his uppercuts with your No Guard,

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:45.650
if you miss a single beat on your Sway Backs, it's all over.

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.100
You got that?

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.420
Yeah, I got that.

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.880
I'm calm now, old man. Something must've gotten into me.

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:05.840
I just got riled up when I saw his thinned-out face smiling like that.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:08.050
But I'm fine now.

00:16:09.570 --> 00:16:12.570
He's gotten so calm so suddenly...

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:24.130
Rikiishi! Don't rush in there! Attack with caution!

00:16:24.130 --> 00:16:27.540
Joe, take your time! Panic, and Rikiishi's gonna get you on the ropes!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:37.510
Go!

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:31.810
Yeah, that's what we've been waiting to see!

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:35.140
The No Guard strategy! I wanted to see that!

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:37.450
Yeah! You got this, Joe the Killer!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:39.760
Dumbass! What are you, a one-trick pony?

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.450
Yabuki! That won't work against Rikiishi!

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:45.750
Don't listen to them, Bro Joe! Pummel that skeleton Rikiishi!

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:48.940
So, you're sticking with uppercuts, just like in the Pancho Leo match, huh, Rikiishi-kun?

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.730
Looks like the Sway Back training made short work of that.

00:18:57.710 --> 00:19:00.910
The first round bell rang just a second ago, Rikiishi-kun.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:24.720
Hit him with a straight! He won't be able to dodge that one!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:28.520
Shut up, amateurs! A straight's just what Yabuki wants him to do!

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:32.020
Your uppercuts aren't even hitting him!

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:39.400
That's it, Joe! Keep hitting him! Keep going!

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.880
R-Rikiishi-kun!

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:14.190
Serves you right.

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:17.670
That's the way, Joe! You're just the man I always knew you were!

00:20:17.670 --> 00:20:19.560
Rikiishi, don't you got any other strategies?

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:21.150
Don't you know any punches besides uppercuts?

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:22.870
Make with the shorts and the hooks!

00:20:22.870 --> 00:20:26.680
Way to go, Joe! You don't have to drag him out! Just take him down!

00:20:26.680 --> 00:20:30.360
What did you think of that first round, Ishida-san? Would you say Yabuki has the advantage?

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:34.380
At this point, I'd say it's Yabuki by four or five points.

00:20:34.380 --> 00:20:37.150
Rikiishi's been missing all his swings, and his posture's crumbling.

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:39.280
Meanwhile, Joe's straights are all hitting their mark.

00:20:39.280 --> 00:20:42.300
I'd say Yabuki's improved his Sway Back a great deal.

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:47.650
I see. But for being in the lead...

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:49.810
Yabuki's got a dull look on his face.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.310
You did well. This match is going pretty good.

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:58.320
You think so?

00:20:58.700 --> 00:21:01.320
What's with that look?

00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.320
I'm in a bad spot in this fight.

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:07.820
A bad spot?

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:09.470
But you had that round in the bag!

00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:11.140
Don't go wussing out on me!

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:15.830
I'm not wussing out. I'm just stating facts.

00:21:16.490 --> 00:21:22.180
Rikiishi's throwing nothing but uppercuts like a one-trick pony, and his posture's weakening!

00:21:22.180 --> 00:21:24.910
Meanwhile, your straights have all hit their mark!

00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:30.600
If you keep this up, you'll have nothing to worry about!

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:34.730
They may be hitting their mark,

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:39.250
but I barely have time to get from the Sway Back to a punching position.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.710
Those punches may be good for points,

00:21:41.710 --> 00:21:43.360
but they didn't do any damage- they just made contact.

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.360
They couldn't even kill a fly.

00:21:50.380 --> 00:21:53.720
It may be a little much to ask at this point,

00:21:53.720 --> 00:21:57.690
but I wouldn't feel right about winning a match by points.

00:21:57.690 --> 00:21:59.720
Especially not against Rikiishi.

00:21:59.720 --> 00:22:01.600
I just don't think I'll be able to avoid his persistent attacks

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:04.300
for all eight rounds of this fight!

00:22:08.210 --> 00:22:12.000
A punch that can hit, but can't even kill a fly. You're exactly right.

00:22:12.000 --> 00:22:18.100
In contrast, Rikiishi has a deadly uppercut that's lethal if it hits even once.

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:22.360
You're right. You're in a bad spot.

00:22:22.700 --> 00:22:27.360
But if you come at him head-on, you'll be more likely to get hit by an uppercut!

00:22:29.130 --> 00:22:32.600
Oh, well. No point in struggling against it now.

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:37.440
I'll bet that my wild instincts can exploit any chance

00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:40.380
that shows up during the fight.

00:22:45.210 --> 00:22:46.830
I'll just have to wait for it.

00:23:21.110 --> 00:23:24.090
Joe's punches couldn't even kill a fly.

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:26.690
And Joe's uneasiness just keeps rising.

00:23:26.690 --> 00:23:32.090
But Rikiishi's uppercuts attack Joe, a dozen times sharper and heavier.

00:23:32.520 --> 00:23:37.320
So Joe decides to switch to the close-quarters-damage strategy.

00:23:37.320 --> 00:23:40.980
He assertively attacks with a string of short hooks.

00:23:40.980 --> 00:23:44.470
But, even as he bleeds, Rikiishi still shows confidence

00:23:44.470 --> 00:23:46.480
and remains a step ahead of Joe.

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:50.660
Now Joe learns what power dwells within Rikiishi.

00:23:50.660 --> 00:23:55.380
And after an intense exchange of blows, Joe is down for the first time!

00:23:55.940 --> 00:24:01.530
Now, as Joe and Rikiishi continue their endless battle to the death,

00:24:01.530 --> 00:24:03.080
which way is tomorrow!?

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:20.060
Yuke kouya wo

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:20.060
Go to the wilderness!

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:23.900
Oira boxer

00:24:21.140 --> 00:24:23.900
I am a boxer.

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:31.650
Yuuhi ga giragira otoko no yume wa

00:24:24.690 --> 00:24:31.650
The evening sun glitters upon the dreams of men!

00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:37.330
Minna wa kono ore wo nasakemuyo to iu

00:24:33.360 --> 00:24:37.330
Everyone says that I am merciless.

